      "writtenOn": "2026-07-08T13:00:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes thats a possibility. In this function, my initial take was that the compiler would opt for a re-read of stack variable than the actual shared memory due to complex function calls after storing it to local new_nent(observable behaviour of a single threaded program may change if any of the called function alter the memory). And hence compiler would not assume that re-read is safe. But if compiler parses all the called functions and verifies that this value is not changed, then its free to re-read it.\n\nYou are right, READ_ONCE() is safest option here.",
